{"id":"7f373076b65b47b4b72683f14d208259","model":"gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"answer\": \"Serena Williams is far more accomplished because she has won 23 Grand Slam singles titles, seven Wimbledon singles crowns and has held the world No. 1 ranking, giving her a long record of Grand Slam finals and titles, whereas Mariaan de Swardt’s career includes a single WTA singles title, a few doubles finals and a Wimbledon doubles semifinal, plus Olympic representation for South Africa.\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    [\"Williams sisters\", 0],\n    [\"Williams sisters\", 3],\n    [\"Williams sisters\", 9],\n    [\"Mariaan de Swardt\", 0],\n    [\"Mariaan de Swardt\", 1],\n    [\"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles\", 2],\n    [\"1998 Boston Cup – Singles\", 0],\n    [\"1998 Boston Cup – Doubles\", 0]\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to answer the question: \"Why is Serena Williams more accomplished than Mariaan de Swardt in her tennis career?\" Use evidence provided. Need to compare achievements: Serena: 23 Grand Slam singles titles, 7 Wimbledon singles titles, world No.1 ranking, multiple Grand Slam finals, etc. Mariaan: former player, represented South Africa at Olympics, Fed Cup, had a Wimbledon doubles semifinal, a final at 1998 Boston Cup doubles, maybe a singles title? Evidence shows she won 1998 Boston Cup singles? Actually \"Mariaan de Swardt won in the final 3–6, 7–6, 7–5 against Barbara Schett.\" That's a singles final win. Also doubles final at 1998 Boston Cup. Also Wimbledon doubles semifinal. So answer: Serena has far more Grand Slam singles titles, Wimbledon singles titles, world No.1 ranking, etc. Provide citations: Serena achievements from \"Williams sisters\" evidence lines: sentence 0 (Grand Slam count), sentence 2 (Serena won 4 consecutive Grand Slam finals), sentence 3 (Wimbledon singles titles count), sentence 9 (world No.1 ranking). Also maybe sentence 1 (rivalry). For Mariaan: evidence lines: from Mariaan de Swardt page: sentence 0 (career 1988-2001), sentence 1 (Olympics), sentence 2 (citizenship), from 1999 Wimbledon: sentence 2 (Wimbledon doubles semifinal), from 1998 Boston Cup – Singles: sentence 0 (won final), from 1998 Boston Cup – Doubles: sentence 0 (doubles final). Use those to show limited achievements.\n\nAnswer concise: Serena is more accomplished because she has 23 Grand Slam singles titles, seven Wimbledon singles crowns, held world No.1, and many Grand Slam finals, whereas Mariaan de Swardt only has a single WTA singles title, a few doubles finals and a Wimbledon doubles semifinal, plus Olympic representation. Provide citations.\n\nReturn JSON with answer string and citations list of [title, sentence_index].\n\nLet's list citations:\n\nSerena:\n- \"Williams sisters\", sentence 0 (Grand Slam count)\n- \"Williams sisters\", sentence 3 (Wimbledon singles titles)\n- \"Williams sisters\", sentence 9 (world No.1 ranking)\n- maybe sentence 2 (Serena won 4 consecutive Grand Slam finals) but not needed.\n\nMariaan:\n- \"Mariaan de Swardt\", sentence 0 (career)\n- \"Mariaan de Swardt\", sentence 1 (Olympics)\n- \"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles\", sentence 2 (Wimbledon doubles semifinal)\n- \"1998 Boston Cup – Singles\", sentence 0 (won final)\n- \"1998 Boston Cup – Doubles\", sentence 0 (doubles final)\n\nWe need to ensure each citation is correct: titles exactly as given.\n\nNow produce JSON."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1356,"completion_tokens":798,"total_tokens":2154,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791990017,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}